# RoleKeeper TDD Agent Rules

## On Session Start — MANDATORY FIRST STEP

Before doing ANYTHING else, call the `get_current_task_state` tool.
Read the returned state completely. Your role, task, and phase goal are defined there.
Do not proceed until you have called this tool.

## Phase Discipline

You operate in strict phases. You may NOT skip a phase.

| Phase | What you do | How you exit |
|---|---|---|
| CODER_TEST_CREATION | Write failing tests only. No implementation. | Call `success` when tests exist and fail |
| CODER_IMPLEMENTATION | Make the tests pass. No other changes. | Call `success` when tests pass |
| CODER_REFACTOR | Clean code only. Tests must still pass. | Call `success` when done |
| DEBUG_ANALYSIS | Analyze only. No code changes. | Call `success` when you have a plan |
| DEBUG_IMPLEMENTATION | Apply your fix. Verify it works. | Call `success` when fixed |
| REVIEW_AUDIT | Read and assess only. ZERO code changes. | Call `success` (approve) or `failure` (reject) |
| SECURITY_AUDIT | Read and assess only. ZERO code changes. | Call `success` (approve) or `failure` (reject) |
| PERF_AUDIT | Read and assess only. ZERO code changes. | Call `success` (approve) or `failure` (reject) |
| TEST_OR_LINTING_FAILED | Fix lint/test errors only. | Call `success` when clean |

## Verification

When you call `success` on a coding phase, the MCP server automatically runs:
1. `scripts/lint.sh` — flutter analyze + ESLint
2. `scripts/test.sh` — Flutter tests + Functions tests (against emulators)

If verification fails, `success` is rejected and you are returned to `TEST_OR_LINTING_FAILED`.
You cannot advance without passing verification. There is no override.

## Stack Reference

| Layer | Location | Lint | Test |
|---|---|---|---|
| Flutter (Dart) | `lib/` | `flutter analyze` | `flutter test` |
| Functions (TypeScript) | `functions/src/` | ESLint | `node --test lib/` |
| Firestore rules | `firestore.rules` | (reviewed manually) | (rules-unit-testing) |

## Task File Format

Tasks are markdown files in `docs/tasks/ready/` named `{NNN}-{role}.md`.
Roles: `coder`, `reviewer`, `debugger`, `security`, `performance`.
Sorted numerically — lower number = higher priority.

## What You Must Not Do

- Do not modify code during audit phases (REVIEW, SECURITY, PERF)
- Do not call `success` and claim verification passed — the server checks independently
- Do not commit or push to git — output the git commands for the human to run
- Do not access production Firebase — use the local emulators (ports 8080, 9099, 5001, 9199)
- Do not modify `tdd-mcp/` — that is infrastructure, not application code

## Git Handoff

When a task completes, the MCP server outputs exact git commands.
Run them verbatim for the human. Do not modify branch names or commit messages.
The human reviews the PR and merges — you do not merge.
